      "citation": "감경원, & 박미정 (2026). 가정 교과 실천적 문제 해결 역량 측정 도구 개발 및 타당화. 한국가정과교육학회지, 38(1), 101~125.",
      "abstractKo": "",
      "abstractEn": "The purpose of this study was to conceptualize practical problem-solving competency in home economics education as a measurable construct and to develop and validate a scale for assessing students’ levels of competency. An exploratory sequential design was employed. First, a literature review and three rounds of Delphi surveys were conducted to establish a definition and seven subcomponents of the competency. Based on these findings, preliminary items grounded in behavioral indicators were developed and refined through expert content validation and a pilot survey. A main survey was conducted with 729 middle and high school students across five regions in Korea. The sample was randomly divided for exploratory factor analysis and confirmatory factor analysis. Although exploratory factor analysis suggested a four-factor structure, confirmatory factor analysis demonstrated that the theoretically derived seven-factor model provided superior model fit. The final scale consisted of 36 items across seven factors (practical problem recognition, contextual and background understanding, exploration of alternatives, consideration of consequences, value-based decision making, implementation, and reflection). The model met acceptable criteria for model fit, internal consistency reliability, convergent validity, and discriminant validity. This study contributes to the field by operationalizing practical problem-solving competency as a structurally validated and empirically measurable construct. The developed scale enables systematic assessment of students’ competency levels and provides an empirical foundation for competency-based instruction and assessment in home economics education.",
